(133105, 6457, 1031, '<td valign="top">Very nice combination of techniques.</td>', 'Very nice combination of techniques.', '2002-10-06 18:43:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(133106, 6457, 4008, '<td valign="top">Thanks for your comments and ratings, 9th place with my first entry, not bad, especially considering it was a lucky shot, just an experiment which ended up with a reflection.<br/>I was trying to make a &amp;lt;A HREF="//www2.photosig.com/viewphoto.php?id=334027" target="blank"  &amp;gt;drop shot&amp;lt;A&amp;gt; by placing a blue glas bowl in the sink and having water drops falling into it. One of the 300 shots caught the splash and because I had not paid enough attention to the background (the comment made by cq107 is absolutely correct) you can see the reflection of the white sink and even the overflow holes. Later shot with a yellow cloth turned up better in terms of color although I did not capture the right moment again. Taken handheld, 1/1000 s, F8, with a home made close-up lens from some lens elements of my old SLR zoom lens (need to use a close-up lens otherwise the camera needs to be to close and gets wet). The color is caused by flashing into the blue glas bowl, the water is just blank water.</td>', 'Thanks for your comments and ratings, 9th place with my first entry, not bad, especially considering it was a lucky shot, just an experiment which ended up with a reflection.I was trying to make a &lt;A HREF="//www2.photosig.com/viewphoto.php?id=334027" target="blank"  &gt;drop shot&lt;A&gt; by placing a blue glas bowl in the sink and having water drops falling into it. One of the 300 shots caught the splash and because I had not paid enough attention to the background (the comment made by cq107 is absolutely correct) you can see the reflection of the white sink and even the overflow holes. Later shot with a yellow cloth turned up better in terms of color although I did not capture the right moment again. Taken handheld, 1/1000 s, F8, with a home made close-up lens from some lens elements of my old SLR zoom lens (need to use a close-up lens otherwise the camera needs to be to close and gets wet). The color is caused by flashing into the blue glas bowl, the water is just blank water.', '2002-10-07 03:51:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(133107, 6458, 2928, '<td valign="top">Great image.  I love the mystic feel of the shot  makes the water look a little crystal ball like. The rose is ghostly, and the bright line looks almost like an intersecting electrical energy force. Colours look great as well.  Only way I think this could be improved is to perhaps crop in a bit closer so that the surrounding area doesn''t draw the eye away. The DOF works well, this helps with the composition; perhaps  I''m nit picking now  cropping just a tiny fraction to left might have helped as well. (7) Good luck.</td>', 'Great image.  I love the mystic feel of the shot  makes the water look a little crystal ball like. The rose is ghostly, and the bright line looks almost like an intersecting electrical energy force. Colours look great as well.  Only way I think this could be improved is to perhaps crop in a bit closer so that the surrounding area doesn''t draw the eye away. The DOF works well, this helps with the composition; perhaps  I''m nit picking now  cropping just a tiny fraction to left might have helped as well. (7) Good luck.', '2002-09-30 10:46:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(133108, 6458, 1280, '<td valign="top">Kind of interesting but I don''t know what I''m looking at.  Is it a turtle in the algae?  Great colors.  Good luck in the challenge.  Grayce aka Gracious</td>', 'Kind of interesting but I don''t know what I''m looking at.  Is it a turtle in the algae?  Great colors.  Good luck in the challenge.  Grayce aka Gracious', '2002-09-30 12:46:00.000000', NULL, 1),
