(133189, 6462, 2618, '<td valign="top">Thanks to all those who ''got'' this picture - my best score yet!<br/><br/>To explain to those who queried/doubted...<br/><br/>There are no shadows in this picture at all, practically the whole thing start to finish is a reflection. The sole exceptions being the mist at the bottom (very subtle, you need to look close) and the downward pointing reeds on the right (I turned the scene upside down to make it look more ''normal). The upward pointing ones are of course their reflection and hence are broken by the ripple. The ripple itself was caused by a Greeb I was actually trying to shoot diving underwater just a little too soon!<br/><br/>Nards, The ''washed out center portion'' is the rising sun! It was very much supposed to be there it being the ''Morning'' part of the title. Oh well, nevermind.<br/><br/>I would like to know why five people gave me a 1 or 2, though. I mean, come on it may not be a perfect picture but it''s surely not THAT bad!<br/><br/>Anyway, I liked this shot and it seems quite a few others did as well. So I''m happy :-).</td>', 'Thanks to all those who ''got'' this picture - my best score yet!To explain to those who queried/doubted...There are no shadows in this picture at all, practically the whole thing start to finish is a reflection. The sole exceptions being the mist at the bottom (very subtle, you need to look close) and the downward pointing reeds on the right (I turned the scene upside down to make it look more ''normal). The upward pointing ones are of course their reflection and hence are broken by the ripple. The ripple itself was caused by a Greeb I was actually trying to shoot diving underwater just a little too soon!Nards, The ''washed out center portion'' is the rising sun! It was very much supposed to be there it being the ''Morning'' part of the title. Oh well, nevermind.I would like to know why five people gave me a 1 or 2, though. I mean, come on it may not be a perfect picture but it''s surely not THAT bad!Anyway, I liked this shot and it seems quite a few others did as well. So I''m happy :-).', '2002-10-07 06:45:00.000000', NULL, 0),
