(133535, 6496, 772, '<td valign="top">Meets the Challenge: Yes<br/>Artistic Merit (Would I print/frame/hang it?): 3<br/>Creativity (Did a lot of thought go into this photo?): 6<br/>Technical (Focus/DOF/Lighting/Etc): 6<br/>Composition (Subject well-positioned and framed): 7<br/>WOW Factor (Is the photo interesting?): 5<br/><br/>Score: 5 - setzler</td>', 'Meets the Challenge: YesArtistic Merit (Would I print/frame/hang it?): 3Creativity (Did a lot of thought go into this photo?): 6Technical (Focus/DOF/Lighting/Etc): 6Composition (Subject well-positioned and framed): 7WOW Factor (Is the photo interesting?): 5Score: 5 - setzler', '2002-10-01 21:04:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(133536, 6496, 2928, '<td valign="top">I like the idea, but I think you should have included the entire window frame and either tilted the camera angle dramatically or remained completely level.  Straight lines in a shot will add calm and diagonals will add drama.  Mixing both often doesn''t work.  This shot is a little halfway between the two worlds. Having pointed out the bad bits, I think the idea is sound, the texture of the window frame works really well, it adds a lot of depth to the shot and the colours all work well together (4) Sorry to score this so low Keep shooting</td>', 'I like the idea, but I think you should have included the entire window frame and either tilted the camera angle dramatically or remained completely level.  Straight lines in a shot will add calm and diagonals will add drama.  Mixing both often doesn''t work.  This shot is a little halfway between the two worlds. Having pointed out the bad bits, I think the idea is sound, the texture of the window frame works really well, it adds a lot of depth to the shot and the colours all work well together (4) Sorry to score this so low Keep shooting', '2002-10-02 06:51:00.000000', NULL, 1),
